# Supertraining (6th Edition, Expanded) — ingest map

PDF is real text: 591 pages, 576 with extractable text (`extract_pdf.py --probe`:
`{"pages": 591, "text_pages": 576, "scanned": false}`), not scanned.

**Print-to-PDF page offset = +11** (PDF page = printed page + 11). Verified at six
independent chapter/section starts, not just the offset's origin point: Ch1 (printed 1 =
PDF 12, "STRENGTH AND THE MUSCULAR SYSTEM"), Ch2 (printed 95 = PDF 106, "SPORT SPECIFIC
STRENGTH TRAINING"), Ch3 (printed 125 = PDF 136, "FACTORS INFLUENCING STRENGTH
PRODUCTION"), Ch4 (printed 201 = PDF 212, "THE MEANS OF SPECIAL STRENGTH TRAINING"), Ch7
(printed 393 = PDF 404, "STRENGTH TRAINING METHODS"), and the Addendum's second section
(printed 563 = PDF 574, "9.2 The Shock Method for Developing Power"). The offset holds
unchanged from the front matter through page 574 of 591; no evidence of a mid-book
repagination (no unnumbered plate inserts were found at the checked points).

**PDF numbers are 0-based:** the "PDF p. N" locators in this book's entries are the
extractor's 0-based page index (printed + 11), matching the offset above. In a normal
1-based PDF viewer (and the Read tool's `pages` parameter), the same page shows as
printed + 12, i.e. one more than the entries' "PDF p." number.

**Confidence rule for this book:** `proven` only for findings that are established,
widely-replicated physiology or mechanics (e.g. force-velocity relationship, motor unit
recruitment order, connective tissue loading response) independent of this text.
Soviet-era empirical findings and training prescriptions original to Verkhoshansky, Siff,
or the Soviet sport-science tradition they cite are capped at `supported`, even when
stated with confidence in the text, because they are largely single-lab or
practice-derived rather than independently replicated in the modern literature available
to this ingest. `contested` is set where modern evidence, or another library book, takes
a different position (e.g. the two-factor fitness-fatigue model vs. classical
supercompensation, already flagged as a live tension in `periodization--bompa`).

